        "is_free": true,
        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Have you ever imagined a sword that moves on its own?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Objective</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you become a sword that moves on its own to become a holy sword. You must run, break through obstacles, and solve troubles to achieve your goal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Blacksmith</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > When the sword's durability is depleted, it will break. You can repair the sword at the blacksmith. You can also collect blueprints and minerals to strengthen yourself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Obstacles and platforms</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you will encounter various platforms. Some will reduce your durability, and some will trick you into stopping your journey to become the holy sword. Do your best to break the obstacles and get over the platforms.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tips</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You will encounter all kinds of hardships and adversities. Sometimes (in fact, most of the time) you will get angry and want to turn off the game. I won't deny it. It could be said that this game was developed to draw out your negative emotions. However, despite this, when you clear the game to the end, your sense of accomplishment will be proportional to your suffering. I wish you good luck on your journey.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Have you ever imagined a sword that moves on its own?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Objective</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you become a sword that moves on its own to become a holy sword. You must run, break through obstacles, and solve troubles to achieve your goal.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Blacksmith</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > When the sword's durability is depleted, it will break. You can repair the sword at the blacksmith. You can also collect blueprints and minerals to strengthen yourself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Obstacles and platforms</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In this game, you will encounter various platforms. Some will reduce your durability, and some will trick you into stopping your journey to become the holy sword. Do your best to break the obstacles and get over the platforms.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tips</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You will encounter all kinds of hardships and adversities. Sometimes (in fact, most of the time) you will get angry and want to turn off the game. I won't deny it. It could be said that this game was developed to draw out your negative emotions. However, despite this, when you clear the game to the end, your sense of accomplishment will be proportional to your suffering. I wish you good luck on your journey.</p>",
